Enhancement: Add the `inventory` command to detect removed or replaced backend objects

The new `inventory` command records the objects physically present in the
repository backend (packs, keys, snapshots and index files) in a local
inventory file given by `--file` or `$RESTIC_INVENTORY_FILE`. On subsequent
runs it reports objects that were removed from the backend and objects that
were replaced (same type and ID but a different size). Objects newly added
by concurrent backups are counted separately and are not reported as
suspicious changes. The inventory file is only replaced atomically after
every object type has been listed successfully, so a failed enumeration can
never overwrite the previous baseline. The command exits with status 1 when
removed or replaced objects were found.
